                },
                "message": "Fix bound cpdef and cdef methods in containers\n\nCalling infer_type() on an AttributeNode after analyse_types() and coerce_to(py_object_type) had already run re-executed analyse_attribute() and reset entry/type back to the unbound C method entry, leaving Python coercion skipped and reading an uninitialized temporary pointer when storing or indexing bound cpdef methods in containers\n\nTrack AttributeNode.analysed once analyse_types() completes attribute resolution so subsequent infer_type() and analyse_types() calls preserve the already-analysed state while keeping the _is_bound_cmethod() guard\n\nAlso keep tuples containing uncoerced bound C or builtin method AttributeNode items as Python tuples in TupleNode.analyse_types() instead of forming invalid or unbound CTupleTypes\n\nCloses #8001",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "77481558fe0126ed2a7cc5f85b141572a165851d",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/trees/77481558fe0126ed2a7cc5f85b141572a165851d"
                },
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/commits/8a7de3f0b1a66b40b7beced7a22474e524621cfc",
                "verification": {
                    "payload": "tree 77481558fe0126ed2a7cc5f85b141572a165851d\nparent 2a4662089231cbfba4bff987fcafa5ca0b62f7eb\nauthor akasakariko <148060537+akasakariko@users.noreply.github.com> 1794749556 +0900\ncommitter akasakariko <148060537+akasakariko@users.noreply.github.com> 1794749556 +0900\n\nFix bound cpdef and cdef methods in containers\n\nCalling infer_type() on an AttributeNode after analyse_types() and coerce_to(py_object_type) had already run re-executed analyse_attribute() and reset entry/type back to the unbound C method entry, leaving Python coercion skipped and reading an uninitialized temporary pointer when storing or indexing bound cpdef methods in containers\n\nTrack AttributeNode.analysed once analyse_types() completes attribute resolution so subsequent infer_type() and analyse_types() calls preserve the already-analysed state while keeping the _is_bound_cmethod() guard\n\nAlso keep tuples containing uncoerced bound C or builtin method AttributeNode items as Python tuples in TupleNode.analyse_types() instead of forming invalid or unbound CTupleTypes\n\nCloses #8001\n",
